WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.370
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and I've just seen around 20 minutes of footage

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.740
from Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.090
I was very lucky to attend a fan event and
also caught some funny moments on camera with

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.030
the cast who were attending, and right now
I'm going to give you a spoiler-free reaction

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.970
to the incredible footage I saw.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.290
If you're new here and a Marvel fan, feel
free to subscribe as I've got tons of Infinity

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.200
War and other MCU videos for you, and there'll
be lots more on the way, including interviews

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.200
with the cast.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.250
Plus, I'll be announcing the winner of my
latest Infinity War giveaway later in this

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.250
video.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.640
To give you some context: the footage I saw
was from the movie's opening act, though it's

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.800
not exactly the beginning of the film.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.140
The clips covered two sequences: one in New
York with Tony Stark, Doctor Strange, Wong,

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.350
Bruce Banner, and more, and the other in space
with the Guardians and Thor.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.470
Bits from some of this footage have already
appeared in the trailers, but obviously we

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.760
got to see a lot more of what happens, and
judging by that, it looks like quite a few

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.810
of my predictions based on the trailers are
on the right path.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:02.030
As you'd expect from the individual movies
featuring these characters, the tone and look

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.390
of each of these scenes is very different.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:08.380
Which is great as it seems like the Russo
Brothers have managed to retain each character

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:13.490
or group's special sense of identity and brought
that nicely into their own mega-packed movie.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.130
There's a ton of humour in both the New York
and Guardians moments.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.130
In fact, these scenes alone feel like they'll
launch a thousand memes, gifs and quotes.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.500
But, of course, this is just 20-or-so minutes
from the early part of a film that's over

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.130
150 minutes long, so I think it's pretty safe
to say that as the stakes rise, the film will

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.400
take on a less comic tone.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.650
What's also fantastic about what I've seen
so far is that there's lots of brilliant interplay

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:37.140
between characters who've spent a good deal
of time together and between characters who've

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.540
never met before; the action is also pretty
special; the music is on point; there's some

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.170
awesome costume reveals; and some cool easter
eggs.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.010
All in all, the footage was a pretty delicious
appetiser for what looks like is going to

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.299
be a totally scrumptious main course!

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:54.440
Roll on the end of April!

